# ── DESIGN REFERENCES ARE NOT COMMITTED, AND THIS REPO IS WHY ───────────────
#
# `docs/design/**/references/` holds screenshots of OTHER COMPANIES' apps,
# curated by Mobbin under their terms. Keeping them in a private repo as
# internal design reference is ordinary practice; publishing them in a PUBLIC
# repo is not ours to do.
#
# github.com/Hama99o/multi_magic_mobile is public, so they stay on disk and out
# of git. Every SPEC.md cites its sources by `mobbin.com/screens/<id>`, which
# does not expire — so the receipts survive in the text even though the images
# do not travel.
#
# If this repo is made private, delete these two lines and commit them.
docs/design/**/references/
docs/design/_review/

# Device screenshots of OUR OWN app are fine to keep, and are the evidence a
# screen is done — but they are large and regenerate from the rig.
docs/design/**/ours/*.png
docs/design/**/ours/*.xml

# @generated expo-cli sync-2b81b286409207a5da26e14c78851eb30d8ccbdb
# The following patterns were generated by expo-cli

expo-env.d.ts
# @end expo-cli
# QA run artefacts — regenerate from the rig; a stale screenshot is worse than none.
qa/reports/*.png
qa/reports/logcat-*.txt

# Same rule as `ours/`, for the same two reasons: they are large, and they
# regenerate from the rig. `qa/evidence/` is the run's own record — every
# picture a flow took, plus the frame and view hierarchy of any step that did
# not hold. The hierarchy dumps are ignored too: they are a snapshot of a real
# session's screen in a PUBLIC repo.
qa/evidence/

# The device claim is machine-local state, not a fact about the repo.
qa/reports/.claims
qa/reports/.claims.lock

# Voice samples for choosing a read-aloud voice: generated audio, 400 KB, and
# this repo is public. On disk to be listened to; SAMPLES.md says how to remake
# them.
docs/read-aloud/samples/
